            {"sentence": "Healthcare demonstrated the steepest rise, surging eightfold from a low of 2 million in 1960 to equal Retail at 16 million by 2020.", "band": "Band 7", "tip": "Calculate multipliers (doubled, tripled, eightfold) when a line shows massive relative growth."},
            {"sentence": "The most notable expansion occurred in Healthcare, which surged from a minimal 2 million in 1960 to 11 million in 2000, before ultimately matching Retail at 16 million in 2020—representing an eightfold overall rise.", "band": "Band 9", "tip": "Emphasize the climax of a trend using relative clauses."},
            {"sentence": "Manufacturing was 15 million in 1960, went to 20 million in 1980, and then went down to 13 million.", "band": "Band 5", "tip": "Combine peak and decline phases: 'Manufacturing peaked at 20 million before entering a continuous decline.'"},
            {"sentence": "Manufacturing held a commanding lead at 15 million positions, peaking at 20 million in 1980 before embarking on a steady downward trajectory.", "band": "Band 9", "tip": "Use terms like 'commanding lead' and 'downward trajectory' to contextualize data."},
